WEBVTT

00:32.240 --> 00:35.952
FIFTIES PROFESSIONALS

00:36.035 --> 00:38.871
15 YEARS AGO

00:40.122 --> 00:41.749
EPISODE 3

00:51.759 --> 00:52.802
You can do it!

01:07.483 --> 01:08.651
Hey, that's enough.

01:11.571 --> 01:12.822
Hey, Chow Yun-fat.

01:13.739 --> 01:16.033
You're not even part of the Hwasan Sect.

01:16.117 --> 01:17.493
This is a fight between your betters

01:17.577 --> 01:21.038
so what the hell is your problem,
jumping in like that?

01:21.581 --> 01:23.374
You've done enough. Now get lost.

01:23.457 --> 01:24.875
You're the ones...

01:25.585 --> 01:27.670
who should get lost
while I'm still asking nicely.

01:28.796 --> 01:32.800
- Oh, yeah?
- He really thinks he's Chow Yun-fat.

01:33.884 --> 01:35.094
Hey, what are you all doing?

01:35.636 --> 01:36.846
Let's wrap this up.

01:48.733 --> 01:49.734
Yes, sir.

01:53.654 --> 01:55.531
Looks like there are
about a dozen of them.

01:58.826 --> 01:59.952
Don't worry.

02:00.953 --> 02:02.455
An hour? No way.

02:03.873 --> 02:04.874
Thirty minutes.

02:06.125 --> 02:08.002
I'll have this cleaned up
and be on my way in 30 minutes.

02:09.795 --> 02:11.631
What the hell is this? Jeez.

02:17.887 --> 02:18.888
Hey.

02:19.764 --> 02:20.890
You a Chow Yun-fat fan too?

02:21.432 --> 02:22.725
Oh, yes.

02:23.476 --> 02:24.477
What's your name?

02:25.353 --> 02:26.562
It's Ma Gong-bok!

02:28.731 --> 02:29.732
Ma Gong-bok.

02:30.566 --> 02:31.567
Nice name.

02:31.984 --> 02:33.069
You like sashimi, right?

02:34.153 --> 02:35.154
Yes!

02:44.705 --> 02:46.123
Let's finish this up quick
and get out of here.

02:46.666 --> 02:48.501
I'll treat you to all the fresh
sashimi you can eat.

02:49.126 --> 02:50.127
Yes!

03:27.915 --> 03:33.421
FIFTIES PROFESSIONALS

03:45.766 --> 03:46.767
Boss!

03:46.976 --> 03:48.436
Let's wrap this up quick
and get out of here.

04:12.376 --> 04:14.170
What are you doing? Go stop him!

04:17.006 --> 04:18.132
Damn it!

04:25.347 --> 04:26.348
Long time no see!

04:32.813 --> 04:34.190
Boss...

04:34.273 --> 04:35.691
Boss!

04:48.245 --> 04:49.246
Jeez.

04:49.872 --> 04:52.208
Beom-ryong, your fists
are as strong as ever.

04:57.129 --> 04:59.048
But you look a little tired.

04:59.381 --> 05:00.549
I'm just getting a little sleepy.

05:01.842 --> 05:03.719
You can't be tired already.

05:04.345 --> 05:06.222
We have to go straight to round two!

05:26.158 --> 05:27.159
Get them!

05:35.793 --> 05:37.336
ORAN CHINESE RESTAURANT

06:22.673 --> 06:24.758
Who are those guys fighting over there?

06:25.718 --> 06:27.219
Wait, that guy...

06:27.761 --> 06:29.305
He's Oldboy, our regular.

06:30.014 --> 06:31.348
What's he doing here?

06:35.728 --> 06:37.521
The young one is the motorcycle owner.

06:38.022 --> 06:39.440
And the other one...

06:40.941 --> 06:42.192
That's Bulgae.

07:44.922 --> 07:45.923
Stomp him!

07:50.719 --> 07:51.720
No.

07:56.684 --> 07:58.936
Stop!

08:11.657 --> 08:13.158
It's all my fault.

08:13.242 --> 08:15.661
Oh, Gong-bok. You stubborn bastard.

08:16.161 --> 08:18.706
After your boss got his ass kicked,
you're finally ready to talk?

08:19.164 --> 08:20.165
Fine, spit it out.

08:20.249 --> 08:22.668
What was the plan behind this whole mess?

08:23.460 --> 08:24.628
Did Chairman Hwang Hwa-san order this?

08:24.712 --> 08:27.548
I'm telling you,
I really don't know who they are!

08:28.007 --> 08:29.008
In-gu.

08:29.091 --> 08:30.718
Can't you see for yourself?

08:31.093 --> 08:33.971
- Beom-ryong's completely lost his edge.
- Ma Gong-bok!

08:34.054 --> 08:36.015
He left that life behind and put
everything into the convenience store.

08:36.223 --> 08:39.018
He hasn't picked a single fight,
not even with the neighborhood punks.

08:39.143 --> 08:41.228
How could Kang Beom-ryong,
a convenience store owner

08:41.854 --> 08:45.691
possibly stand up
to a big boss like you, Yoo In-gu?

08:46.567 --> 08:47.985
For old times' sake...

08:48.193 --> 08:49.945
please let this go just this once.

08:50.237 --> 08:52.239
Damn, look at this shameless bastard.

08:53.949 --> 08:55.993
I'd like to grind you into dust

08:56.076 --> 08:57.077
and you're asking for old times' sake?

08:57.161 --> 08:58.370
I'm not letting you off easy.

08:58.454 --> 09:00.164
No, don't!

09:00.289 --> 09:01.582
Yoo In-gu, don't!

09:02.541 --> 09:05.836
You only need one arm
to scan barcodes at a convenience store.

09:05.919 --> 09:07.504
- No, don't!
- Grab him.

09:07.588 --> 09:08.714
No! I need both arms!

09:08.797 --> 09:10.257
I need both hands!

09:10.591 --> 09:12.509
In-gu! I mean...

09:12.885 --> 09:14.428
Boss. Sir!

09:14.553 --> 09:15.804
This was all my fault.

09:15.888 --> 09:17.347
I didn't know my place.

09:17.806 --> 09:19.266
I overstepped my bounds.

09:19.349 --> 09:21.393
It's all my fault. I apologize.

09:21.643 --> 09:22.644
So please...

09:23.103 --> 09:25.230
just give us one more chance. If you do...

09:26.398 --> 09:28.108
we'll do anything you say.

09:29.443 --> 09:30.444
Anything?

09:36.158 --> 09:37.451
Then bark like a dog.

09:44.416 --> 09:45.709
- Woof, woof!
- Boss!

09:45.793 --> 09:46.919
Woof, woof!

09:47.002 --> 09:49.046
Woof, woof!

09:51.090 --> 09:52.674
I'll bark instead!

09:53.217 --> 09:54.676
Woof, woof, woof, woof!

09:54.760 --> 09:57.387
Woof, woof, woof, woof, woof!

09:57.471 --> 09:58.972
Woof, woof, woof, woof!

09:59.056 --> 10:02.142
Woof, woof, woof, woof, woof!

10:02.226 --> 10:03.227
Woof!

10:05.312 --> 10:06.355
Stop it!

10:07.481 --> 10:09.608
Woof, woof, woof!

10:10.859 --> 10:15.280
Woof, woof, woof! Woof, woof, woof!

10:15.364 --> 10:16.865
Woof, woof, woof!

10:23.539 --> 10:24.748
Shut up!

10:31.171 --> 10:33.465
This is so touching,
it's making me tear up.

10:34.091 --> 10:36.343
Get them. Finish them off
before I change my mind.

10:36.718 --> 10:38.095
- We barked!
- No!

10:38.178 --> 10:39.680
I barked!

10:39.763 --> 10:41.431
We barked!

10:42.391 --> 10:43.392
You bastard.

10:43.684 --> 10:44.685
Hold on.

10:45.769 --> 10:47.354
Sergeant Kim, what is it?
I'm busy right now.

10:47.437 --> 10:49.523
Sir, are you at Yeongseon Food
by any chance?

10:49.690 --> 10:52.651
An anonymous assault report
was just filed at Yeongseon Food.

10:52.734 --> 10:54.736
If a unit is dispatched now,
they'll be there in ten minutes.

10:54.903 --> 10:56.738
A report? Which bastard did it?

10:56.947 --> 10:58.991
Please, just call it a day and wrap it up.

10:59.074 --> 11:00.784
Hey, can't you even cover up
something like this?

11:00.993 --> 11:02.536
You should at least be worth
what I pay you, damn it.

11:03.495 --> 11:06.498
The report has already been filed.
There's nothing I can do.

11:06.748 --> 11:08.083
For now, just get out of there.

11:08.167 --> 11:09.835
I'll delay the dispatch as long as I can.

11:21.096 --> 11:22.347
Hey, Kang Beom-ryong.

11:23.015 --> 11:26.059
If you're just a country mutt,
wear a leash and guard a house.

11:26.560 --> 11:29.521
Stop wandering around causing trouble,
unless you want to get yourself killed.

11:38.280 --> 11:39.281
But.

11:40.324 --> 11:42.701
It's been too long
to say goodbye like this, right?

11:49.333 --> 11:51.210
Boss, are you okay?

11:55.923 --> 11:56.924
YEONGSEON FOOD

11:57.007 --> 11:59.301
THE PRIDE OF KOREA PORK PREMIUM JERKY
YEONGSEON FOOD

12:07.893 --> 12:08.894
- Oh, my back.
- Boss, are you okay?

12:09.019 --> 12:11.230
Gosh, get this off me.

12:19.655 --> 12:20.656
Why won't this come off?

12:20.989 --> 12:21.990
Are you okay?

12:34.920 --> 12:36.630
I'm giving you exactly three days.

12:36.713 --> 12:38.006
If you're not out by then

12:38.090 --> 12:39.549
we're forcibly demolishing this place.

12:39.633 --> 12:41.468
Forced demolition, sir?

12:42.302 --> 12:44.680
And if you want to report this,
go right ahead.

12:45.138 --> 12:47.683
But who do you think is faster?
The cops or us?

12:48.225 --> 12:49.685
If you're curious, give it a try.

12:49.768 --> 12:50.978
You get what I'm saying, high schooler?

12:52.020 --> 12:53.814
- Nam-il...
- Let's go.

12:54.731 --> 12:56.275
Nam-il.

12:56.650 --> 13:00.070
Nam-il, Nam-il.

13:00.153 --> 13:02.072
Are you okay? Nam-il.

13:02.698 --> 13:05.284
- Nam-il, are you okay?
- Uncle...

13:05.993 --> 13:07.244
They're gone.

13:07.327 --> 13:08.328
Uncle...

13:08.954 --> 13:10.122
They're gone...

13:15.669 --> 13:16.670
Boss.

13:16.753 --> 13:18.338
If you're really worried...

13:18.755 --> 13:20.382
should I get some skilled guys

13:20.716 --> 13:22.217
to put the screws on him?

13:22.884 --> 13:24.177
Skilled guys?

13:24.261 --> 13:26.138
That Kang Beom-ryong guy

13:26.221 --> 13:27.848
he seems to have lost his bite

13:27.931 --> 13:29.141
so why don't we wait for the right moment

13:29.224 --> 13:30.726
and take care of him quietly?

13:33.228 --> 13:34.229
ONE UNREAD MESSAGE

13:34.313 --> 13:36.481
KIM BANG-GON
I JUST ARRIVED AT CHAIRMAN DO'S CASINO

13:38.275 --> 13:39.276
Forget it.

13:39.359 --> 13:40.736
We need to lay low for a while.

13:41.737 --> 13:43.363
He's at Chairman Do's casino right now.

13:43.447 --> 13:44.448
Chairman Do?

13:44.698 --> 13:45.782
Isn't he on a business trip in the States?

13:45.866 --> 13:48.702
I don't know. What is that sly fox
plotting by coming back like this?

13:49.828 --> 13:51.788
We need to keep an eye
on Chairman Do for a while.

13:51.872 --> 13:53.832
- You know what I mean?
- Understood, Boss.

13:54.291 --> 13:55.959
Anyway, that bastard Kang Beom-ryong...

13:56.043 --> 13:57.919
he's got some damn good luck.

14:22.277 --> 14:23.987
I told you, if you're tired,
get some rest.

14:24.613 --> 14:25.614
No, I'm fine.

14:26.406 --> 14:27.532
You must be tired too.

14:28.325 --> 14:29.409
Tired? Please.

14:29.493 --> 14:32.537
You think a few weak punches
like that would faze me?

14:32.913 --> 14:35.207
I just didn't get any sleep last night

14:35.290 --> 14:36.666
so I was a little off my game.

14:37.542 --> 14:38.794
If I hadn't frozen up

14:38.877 --> 14:41.296
I would've wiped the floor
with those bastards, damn it.

14:46.051 --> 14:47.094
I'm sorry.

14:48.762 --> 14:50.138
What's with the sudden apology?
That's not like you.

14:50.222 --> 14:52.057
Because I went after Jeong Ho-myeong...

14:52.933 --> 14:55.394
I ended up dragging Yoo In-gu into this.

14:55.894 --> 14:57.938
From now on, I'm going to
stop chasing Jeong Ho-myeong

14:58.355 --> 14:59.564
and getting revenge for the Chairman...

15:00.399 --> 15:02.567
I'm giving it all up.

15:03.985 --> 15:04.986
What?

15:05.904 --> 15:07.948
- What? Why?
- The one who ruined Heaven Capital

15:08.156 --> 15:09.574
wasn't Jeong Ho-myeong.

15:10.909 --> 15:12.035
God, seriously.

15:12.285 --> 15:13.995
I was such an idiot to get it wrong.

15:14.246 --> 15:16.081
And now Yoo In-gu is on our tail.

15:16.665 --> 15:18.041
No, but really...

15:18.125 --> 15:19.251
I think just forgetting

15:19.543 --> 15:21.294
about the past and moving on

15:21.837 --> 15:22.879
is the only way.

15:23.880 --> 15:25.465
You're really just going to forget it all?

15:25.549 --> 15:26.550
Yes.

15:26.800 --> 15:29.136
Like you said, from now on I'll just...

15:29.928 --> 15:30.971
live a normal life.

15:31.555 --> 15:32.764
Just working at the convenience store.

15:33.849 --> 15:35.434
I'll try my best to live that way.

15:43.233 --> 15:44.401
Good grief.

15:45.694 --> 15:48.113
Well, have a good one.

15:50.490 --> 15:52.159
Don't go. Hey, where are you going?

15:53.869 --> 15:54.870
Gong-bok.

15:58.665 --> 15:59.708
What...

16:00.125 --> 16:01.793
- Was the convenience store robbed?
- Sorry?

16:02.794 --> 16:04.463
No, I mean...

16:04.546 --> 16:06.047
- your face!
- No.

16:06.715 --> 16:09.134
Oh, no. This? It's nothing.

16:14.848 --> 16:16.224
Was it gangsters?

16:18.977 --> 16:20.854
Gangsters?

16:21.480 --> 16:22.481
No, that's not it.

16:22.564 --> 16:24.691
I've been seeing a lot of gangsters around
the casino lately.

16:25.525 --> 16:27.277
You're having trouble with them,
aren't you?

16:27.360 --> 16:30.780
- Those bastards!
- No! No, it's not like that.

16:31.031 --> 16:32.199
I'm sorry.

16:32.282 --> 16:33.533
It wasn't gangsters.

16:33.617 --> 16:36.036
It was just some drunk customers
making a scene.

16:36.119 --> 16:37.829
But I talked them down

16:37.913 --> 16:39.164
so you really don't need to report it.

16:42.125 --> 16:44.085
- But still...
- Oh, right!

16:44.169 --> 16:46.087
You're here for a lunch box, aren't you?

16:46.296 --> 16:47.589
I wonder if any of these are okay.

17:06.691 --> 17:09.444
That wound could get infected
if you're not careful.

17:19.913 --> 17:21.164
Even if you don't report it

17:21.248 --> 17:22.707
you should at least treat it.

17:25.710 --> 17:26.711
Treat it...

17:28.630 --> 17:29.798
Anyway...

17:29.881 --> 17:31.675
whether it's drunks or gangsters

17:31.758 --> 17:33.510
people who just throw their weight around

17:33.593 --> 17:36.596
and hurt people should be
taken off the streets.

17:36.680 --> 17:38.890
So if this happens again

17:38.974 --> 17:40.600
you have to report it.

17:41.268 --> 17:42.269
Okay.

17:42.352 --> 17:43.353
And...

17:43.853 --> 17:46.022
if you feel uncomfortable reporting...

17:47.899 --> 17:49.317
you can call me directly.

17:50.652 --> 17:51.945
JUSTICE IS ALIVE
OFFICER PARK MI-KYUNG

17:52.028 --> 17:54.656
I didn't know police officers carried
business cards like these.

17:54.739 --> 17:56.032
I had them made myself.

17:56.324 --> 17:57.534
It's a limited edition of 100.

17:57.617 --> 17:59.744
Wow, a limited edition. This is valuable.

17:59.828 --> 18:00.829
Why give one to me?

18:00.912 --> 18:03.123
Hard-working citizens like you

18:03.999 --> 18:05.875
are who police officers
like me are here to protect.

18:05.959 --> 18:07.294
So please...

18:07.586 --> 18:08.712
be sure to call.

18:09.379 --> 18:10.839
Call me.

18:11.381 --> 18:13.717
- Okay.
- Okay.

18:17.679 --> 18:18.680
Take care.

18:28.023 --> 18:29.065
I'm sorry, Boss.

18:30.025 --> 18:31.443
Go and find happiness

18:32.027 --> 18:33.612
in an ordinary life.

18:34.821 --> 18:35.905
What I started...

18:36.781 --> 18:38.867
I'll finish myself.

18:40.785 --> 18:42.245
What? Are you sure?

18:42.329 --> 18:43.622
It was Bulgae?

18:44.080 --> 18:45.206
I'm sure.

18:45.832 --> 18:47.500
The dress he wore

18:47.584 --> 18:49.252
on the ferry ten years ago

18:49.336 --> 18:50.378
was in his house.

18:50.545 --> 18:52.380
What about the item? Did you find it too?

18:52.839 --> 18:54.633
I searched everywhere

18:55.884 --> 18:57.302
but the receiver wasn't responding.

18:58.845 --> 19:00.180
I don't think it's in the house.

19:01.264 --> 19:03.767
I think we need to take a different

19:04.309 --> 19:06.144
more careful approach.

19:06.227 --> 19:07.562
Why?

19:07.646 --> 19:08.688
Is something wrong?

19:09.147 --> 19:10.482
Do you think Bulgae is just some nobody?

19:11.316 --> 19:13.068
He stayed on Yeongseon Island
for ten years

19:13.151 --> 19:14.653
and even got a job.

19:15.570 --> 19:17.739
And he infiltrated that family
with the grandchild.

19:18.198 --> 19:19.449
It could be a trap.

19:19.991 --> 19:20.992
A trap?

19:21.076 --> 19:22.285
At Yeongseon Food...

19:22.911 --> 19:24.871
Bulgae wasn't the only one there.

19:26.414 --> 19:27.791
The guy with the forehead scar

19:27.874 --> 19:29.918
the high school kid, the hick.

19:30.335 --> 19:31.503
And...

19:32.045 --> 19:34.297
the regular, Oldboy.

19:34.964 --> 19:37.884
Him being with Bulgae just doesn't add up.

19:38.385 --> 19:39.636
It could be a coincidence.

19:39.969 --> 19:41.596
The guy's been lurking around me
for ten years

19:41.680 --> 19:44.349
and he just happens to be getting
beaten up with Bulgae?

19:44.432 --> 19:45.433
You know it too.

19:45.517 --> 19:46.518
At that time...

19:46.768 --> 19:48.103
there was a third person.

19:49.479 --> 19:51.523
Let's start by digging into
what's right in front of us

19:51.606 --> 19:53.358
one step at a time.

19:54.150 --> 19:55.568
This Oldboy guy...

19:56.277 --> 19:57.654
I'll go have a talk with him.

19:58.363 --> 19:59.447
Ho-myeong.

19:59.698 --> 20:01.700
We're so close. Be careful.

20:01.908 --> 20:02.992
This is your first mission in ten years.

20:03.076 --> 20:04.703
Oh, come on!

20:05.704 --> 20:06.830
Have you forgotten who I am?

20:32.063 --> 20:34.733
SEPTEMBER 2010

22:08.159 --> 22:10.662
Going with the classic method, are we?

22:24.092 --> 22:26.052
MANAGER LEE

22:29.806 --> 22:31.349
- Hello?
- Manager Bong.

22:31.850 --> 22:34.310
You can't just not show up
for work without calling.

22:34.394 --> 22:35.645
Manager Lee.

22:36.437 --> 22:38.982
I'm feeling really sick.

22:41.276 --> 22:44.195
Look, I can't cover for you anymore.

22:44.279 --> 22:46.489
I'll be there tomorrow
even if I have to crawl in.

22:46.573 --> 22:47.699
Just this one time...

22:47.782 --> 22:49.158
If you continue to have

22:49.450 --> 22:51.661
unexcused absences,
you will be terminated.

22:51.911 --> 22:54.122
I... I really...

23:04.382 --> 23:05.383
Damn it.

23:53.473 --> 23:55.516
JUSTICE IS ALIVE
OFFICER PARK MI-KYUNG

23:57.852 --> 24:00.480
JUSTICE IS ALIVE
OFFICER PARK MI-KYUNG

24:18.331 --> 24:22.043
JUMBO24
FRIENDLY CONVENIENCE STORE

24:22.126 --> 24:28.883
YEONGSEON POLICE SUBSTATION

24:52.573 --> 24:53.574
Sir.

24:53.658 --> 24:54.826
What are you doing, kid?

24:56.452 --> 24:57.662
Are you going to a wedding?

25:00.456 --> 25:01.457
Yes.

25:02.542 --> 25:03.710
I'm going far away.

25:06.004 --> 25:07.005
Listen, sir.

25:08.589 --> 25:09.590
I...

25:11.718 --> 25:13.511
made sure to stock up on Seoraksan.

25:14.303 --> 25:15.555
So I hope you'll continue

25:15.638 --> 25:16.931
to shop here...

25:18.224 --> 25:19.225
here at our store.

25:20.226 --> 25:21.227
Please.

25:22.311 --> 25:23.312
What's gotten into you?

25:53.051 --> 25:54.135
Surprise!

25:54.385 --> 25:56.304
- You're early, President Yoo.
- Early?

25:56.387 --> 25:58.014
You drag me out here at the crack of dawn

25:58.097 --> 25:59.432
and you're just stuffing your face?

25:59.515 --> 26:00.808
You're still a real piece of work.

26:00.892 --> 26:02.310
A leopard can't change its spots.

26:02.393 --> 26:03.853
Want some brunch?

26:04.145 --> 26:07.148
CHAIRMAN OF HEAVEN HOTEL AND CASINO
DO HYEON-TAE

26:07.231 --> 26:08.566
Are you trying to give me an ulcer?

26:08.941 --> 26:10.109
Just get to the point.

26:11.569 --> 26:12.570
Okay.

26:14.530 --> 26:15.531
All right.

26:15.615 --> 26:17.408
I'll get right to business. Have a seat.

26:17.700 --> 26:18.701
Hey, Director.

26:20.328 --> 26:21.329
All right.

26:27.794 --> 26:30.046
I heard you beat up my security staff
a few days ago.

26:30.713 --> 26:32.799
I mean, how can you
treat salaried employees

26:32.882 --> 26:34.926
like they're some street punks?

26:35.134 --> 26:36.511
A man in your position should know better.

26:36.594 --> 26:39.222
Damn it. I was trying
to be nice about this.

26:40.848 --> 26:42.266
So what? You want me to
pay their medical bills?

26:42.350 --> 26:44.018
No! No.

26:44.602 --> 26:47.063
I can take care of their medical bills.

26:48.439 --> 26:50.733
But something just occurred to me.

26:51.818 --> 26:52.819
Why?

26:53.444 --> 26:54.987
I don't understand. Why?

26:56.072 --> 26:58.533
Don't give me that English crap
and speak Korean.

26:58.616 --> 27:01.327
Why would you go so far
as to beat up my security staff

27:01.410 --> 27:03.287
just to check the CCTV footage?

27:03.746 --> 27:05.414
What exactly was on that footage?

27:07.166 --> 27:09.669
Is there some kind of problem

27:09.752 --> 27:11.546
at Heaven Capital?
That's what I'm wondering.

27:12.505 --> 27:13.714
Stop trying to test me.

27:13.798 --> 27:14.799
Test you?

27:15.133 --> 27:17.677
Come on, why would I test you?
I don't have time for that.

27:18.636 --> 27:21.389
President Yoo, any problem
with your business?

27:21.931 --> 27:23.933
- Stupid.
- You wannabe Yankee bastard.

27:24.016 --> 27:25.601
I told you to speak Korean! Damn it.

27:32.400 --> 27:34.110
This bastard... Damn it.

27:35.778 --> 27:36.779
This guy...

27:41.826 --> 27:43.578
Whoa, calm down.

27:43.661 --> 27:45.079
Calm down, man. Director Nam.

27:47.206 --> 27:49.208
Jeez, why is everyone so worked up?

27:49.417 --> 27:50.459
Huh? It's so vulgar.

27:51.043 --> 27:53.588
I was just asking out of
concern for you, President Yoo.

27:53.713 --> 27:55.131
- Concern?
- Yeah.

27:55.715 --> 27:56.716
President Yoo.

27:56.966 --> 27:59.385
Heaven Capital, your business, but...

27:59.552 --> 28:02.138
Heaven Hotel and Casino,
my business. So...

28:02.847 --> 28:04.599
We're in the same boat here,
called Heaven.

28:04.682 --> 28:05.975
If you cause trouble

28:06.058 --> 28:07.226
and word gets back to Chief Han

28:07.310 --> 28:09.437
it'll be a problem for both of us, okay?

28:09.854 --> 28:12.231
We're co-workers in the same boat. Right?

28:12.565 --> 28:14.317
When trouble comes,
we gotta help each other, right?

28:14.400 --> 28:16.527
Help me? You?

28:17.111 --> 28:18.529
What a load of bullshit.

28:18.863 --> 28:20.865
You'd be the first one to
take over my business if I go down.

28:23.868 --> 28:25.494
I'll handle this myself

28:25.745 --> 28:27.663
so just shut your mouth. Got it?

28:28.122 --> 28:29.749
Oh, "shut my mouth."

28:30.625 --> 28:31.626
Okay.

28:31.834 --> 28:32.835
No problem.

28:33.461 --> 28:34.462
Bye.

28:35.254 --> 28:36.339
He won't even accept my help.

28:40.927 --> 28:41.928
Well.

28:44.931 --> 28:47.141
President Yoo's drug-laced beef jerky
is going around the casino.

28:47.475 --> 28:48.476
Drugs?

28:53.439 --> 28:54.815
Damn.

28:55.107 --> 28:56.317
President Yoo has been busy.

28:56.525 --> 28:58.444
I think getting involved
could be a problem.

28:59.153 --> 29:00.363
Should I report this to Chief Han?

29:07.453 --> 29:08.579
For now...

29:09.038 --> 29:10.748
let's just keep this to ourselves.

29:13.125 --> 29:14.126
Instead...

29:15.086 --> 29:16.254
why don't we

29:16.337 --> 29:19.298
take a closer look at this jerky business?

29:19.757 --> 29:21.384
If the business model is solid

29:21.467 --> 29:23.344
it wouldn't be a bad idea
for us to take it over.

29:23.844 --> 29:26.097
And keep a close eye
on the Heaven Capital situation.

29:26.180 --> 29:28.599
Yes, I'll look into it and report back.

29:41.404 --> 29:43.322
I told you to make sure the security team
kept their mouths shut.

29:43.531 --> 29:44.865
Can't you do one thing right?

29:45.366 --> 29:47.743
You might as well advertise
that we have a problem.

29:48.035 --> 29:49.078
I'm sorry, sir.

29:49.912 --> 29:50.997
You little...

29:57.962 --> 29:59.672
Stop following me
and get the car. Damn it.

30:03.801 --> 30:06.178
The number you have dialed is unavailable.
Please leave a message...

30:40.546 --> 30:42.131
I've had enough.

30:42.882 --> 30:45.509
- That's enough.
- Take more!

31:17.500 --> 31:19.627
Are you from a newspaper?

31:20.336 --> 31:21.879
Or a TV station?

31:22.088 --> 31:23.130
Hello.

31:23.214 --> 31:25.758
I'm sorry. I should have
introduced myself sooner.

31:26.217 --> 31:28.177
I'm from the Criminal Division of the
Imcheon District Prosecutors' Office

31:28.928 --> 31:30.262
Prosecutor Gang Yeong-ae.

31:32.556 --> 31:34.517
I'd like to ask you a few questions.

31:34.600 --> 31:36.018
What would a prosecutor want

31:36.102 --> 31:38.062
with a washed-up old man like me?

31:38.687 --> 31:41.065
I've just been cooped up in my room

31:41.148 --> 31:44.026
so I don't know much
about the outside world.

31:44.110 --> 31:45.319
Ten years ago.

31:45.653 --> 31:47.738
the murder of the
National Security Advisor, Kwon Soon-bok.

31:48.197 --> 31:50.866
It's the case that put you in prison

31:50.950 --> 31:52.118
so you should know more
about it than anyone.

31:52.201 --> 31:54.370
That case is closed.

31:55.955 --> 31:57.581
So why are you asking about it?

31:57.665 --> 31:59.667
If the real culprit was never caught...

32:00.459 --> 32:02.002
then the case isn't closed, is it?

32:02.837 --> 32:05.756
And I'm not talking about it
being a personal grudge.

32:06.048 --> 32:08.175
Or that it was ordered by one of
Kwon Soon-bok's political rivals.

32:08.259 --> 32:10.136
Forget those tabloid rumors.

32:11.178 --> 32:13.180
Please tell me the truth.

32:14.140 --> 32:15.766
The person who framed you for murder

32:15.850 --> 32:18.811
and put you in prison...

32:21.814 --> 32:23.149
was this person, wasn't it?

32:31.657 --> 32:34.160
I don't know what you're talking about.

32:34.702 --> 32:35.703
Jeez...

32:36.078 --> 32:39.498
- Mr. Hwang Hwa-san.
- If you're going to use tabloid stories

32:39.957 --> 32:41.709
at least pick a believable one.

32:43.210 --> 32:44.211
Good grief.

32:44.462 --> 32:46.255
Are you really that scared
of Han Gyeong-wook?

32:55.431 --> 32:56.682
Prosecutor.

32:57.016 --> 32:59.643
I lost the organization
I spent my entire life building

32:59.727 --> 33:02.646
and now I'm rotting
in a cell in my old age.

33:02.730 --> 33:04.398
At this point...

33:04.857 --> 33:06.984
what could I possibly
have to be afraid of?

33:08.319 --> 33:11.739
I'm just tired of being used
and getting nothing in return.

33:11.822 --> 33:15.201
That's what I can't stand.

33:17.036 --> 33:18.579
I'm not trying to use you.

33:19.163 --> 33:21.248
I'm proposing a win-win situation.

33:21.499 --> 33:22.833
I need to solve this case.

33:22.917 --> 33:25.127
And you need a chance to get out of here.

33:28.547 --> 33:30.216
For it to be a win-win...

33:30.841 --> 33:35.387
shouldn't I get out of prison first?

33:36.722 --> 33:39.934
Bring me the person who really killed
Chief Kwon Soon-bok.

33:41.227 --> 33:44.104
Then we'll talk.

33:48.817 --> 33:50.194
So you do know who the real killer is.

33:53.489 --> 33:54.907
Who is it?

34:00.579 --> 34:02.498
It wasn't...

34:02.957 --> 34:04.959
a person.

34:05.876 --> 34:08.087
It was a mutt...

34:09.630 --> 34:11.549
that I raised.

34:20.182 --> 34:22.977
Damn, she's scurrying all over the place.

34:23.185 --> 34:24.520
She's not Nongae, she's a stray dog.

34:25.396 --> 34:26.897
Should I report in now?

34:27.439 --> 34:28.607
Hold on.

34:28.857 --> 34:30.526
Let's see where she's headed first.

34:42.288 --> 34:44.582
RESTRICTED NUMBER

34:50.796 --> 34:52.089
This is Prosecutor Gang Yeong-ae.

34:52.172 --> 34:53.257
Prosecutor Gang.

34:53.340 --> 34:55.676
Poking your nose around
isn't going to solve anything.

34:56.135 --> 34:58.887
You should be watching your back.

34:59.346 --> 35:01.557
- Who is this?
- I can't tell you that yet.

35:02.057 --> 35:03.642
The people in the white car
ahead of you...

35:04.351 --> 35:05.352
don't they look familiar?

35:11.942 --> 35:12.943
You see the road ahead?

35:13.360 --> 35:14.987
Go straight through the intersection.

35:15.279 --> 35:16.780
I'll take care of the rest.

35:16.864 --> 35:18.073
Wait. Hello?

35:32.504 --> 35:35.007
ESTABLISHING LAW AND ORDER

35:58.447 --> 36:00.115
- Hey, what the...
- Ma'am.

36:00.199 --> 36:01.492
- What's going on?
- Are you okay?

36:01.575 --> 36:03.160
We're the police.

36:03.619 --> 36:04.828
- Excuse me.
- Ma'am.

36:04.953 --> 36:06.747
Ma'am, are you okay? Ma'am?

36:06.955 --> 36:08.290
- Excuse me.
- Hello, ma'am?

36:08.374 --> 36:09.625
- Hello?
- What should we do?

36:12.336 --> 36:13.420
What?

36:13.504 --> 36:14.505
What is happening?

36:14.880 --> 36:16.590
What's with her?

36:17.216 --> 36:18.217
Mister.

36:18.425 --> 36:19.426
What the...

36:38.737 --> 36:39.738
Nice to meet you.

36:40.489 --> 36:41.490
Hello.

36:42.408 --> 36:43.659
- It's a pleasure to meet you.
- Hello.

36:45.119 --> 36:46.120
Thank you for coming all this way.

36:46.203 --> 36:47.621
I'll escort you inside.

36:58.382 --> 37:00.759
Why does it have to be so
meticulous and long-winded...

37:01.343 --> 37:05.514
VICE PRESIDENT, TOYO FINANCE, TOKYO
RYUSEIGUMI CLAN YAKUZA, NAKATOMO RYUICHI

37:09.351 --> 37:11.395
HEAD OF FUTURE STRATEGY, HUNAN
CONSTRUCTION, CHINESE TRIAD EXECUTIVE

37:11.478 --> 37:13.147
LI GUOFENG

37:13.439 --> 37:15.441
The project hasn't even started.

37:16.191 --> 37:17.985
That's what it says, right?

37:18.193 --> 37:21.780
Land acquisition usually involves
a lot of procedures

37:21.905 --> 37:22.990
and it’s already been several months.

37:23.157 --> 37:24.241
But I heard that

37:24.324 --> 37:26.535
the city government
is still delaying the approval.

37:27.077 --> 37:30.414
I’m starting to question whether
you’re actually capable of handling this.

37:34.793 --> 37:37.796
It's true that
the project has been delayed

37:38.088 --> 37:39.882
but this was something
we fully anticipated.

37:40.382 --> 37:42.801
Once I win the mayoral election

37:42.885 --> 37:45.345
the permit issues
will be resolved immediately.

37:45.596 --> 37:49.224
After that, the project will begin
to gain momentum

37:49.600 --> 37:50.851
so I ask for your patience

37:51.602 --> 37:52.603
and to just wait and see.

37:54.813 --> 37:56.023
Of course.

37:56.940 --> 38:02.905
The difference in approval ratings
between them is only 0.5%.

38:03.322 --> 38:06.700
Can you really say
with certainty that he will win?

38:06.867 --> 38:12.289
And I've heard that the opposing candidate
has strong connections to Imcheon.

38:13.791 --> 38:16.335
Isn't it entirely possible
for things to be overturned?

38:33.143 --> 38:34.228
What about Kim Seon-jung?

38:35.354 --> 38:36.814
He's proving to be
more difficult than we expected.

38:37.064 --> 38:38.440
No matter how much
we dig through his accounts

38:38.524 --> 38:40.108
we can't find any dirt on him.

38:40.818 --> 38:42.361
REPORT ON CANDIDATE KIM SEON-JUNG

38:42.444 --> 38:44.279
And there's nothing
we can turn into a scandal?

38:44.363 --> 38:46.240
Ever since his days as a teacher
on Yeongseon Island

38:46.323 --> 38:48.158
he's been highly respected by everyone.

38:48.242 --> 38:50.077
We couldn't even find a single rumor
about him taking bribes.

38:50.577 --> 38:51.995
We looked into his relationships

38:52.079 --> 38:53.831
but his only family is his wife.

38:54.248 --> 38:57.042
His wife is the director of an
orphanage called Jaae Won

38:57.292 --> 38:58.544
and she also has an excellent reputation.

38:59.878 --> 39:02.464
So he's lived a squeaky-clean life?

39:03.966 --> 39:05.175
DEPOSIT AND WITHDRAWL RECORDS
OF KIM SEON-JUNG IN THE LAST YEAR

39:05.259 --> 39:06.844
Kim Seon-jung also acts as a sponsor

39:06.927 --> 39:10.472
and he seems to have a special interest
in the orphanage.

39:12.850 --> 39:14.226
Should we dig a little deeper
into that connection?

39:14.935 --> 39:16.353
Just arrange a meeting.

39:18.105 --> 39:20.482
No matter how squeaky clean he is

39:20.816 --> 39:22.818
it only takes a few storms
to turn the water muddy...

39:23.235 --> 39:24.319
It happens in an instant.

39:25.445 --> 39:26.697
Set it up as soon as possible.

39:27.322 --> 39:28.323
Yes, sir.

39:50.846 --> 39:51.889
Oh, hello.

39:51.972 --> 39:54.600
You're Mr. Jeong
from Oran Chinese Restaurant, right?

39:54.683 --> 39:56.351
Wow, it's great to see you.

39:56.435 --> 39:58.896
But... why am I tied up like this?

39:59.229 --> 40:01.356
"You're Mr. Jeong
from Oran Chinese Restaurant, right?"

40:04.651 --> 40:08.697
I should've known when you kept ordering
those unpopular fried dumplings.

40:09.197 --> 40:10.198
What?

40:10.657 --> 40:12.409
Sir, what do you mean by that?

40:12.492 --> 40:14.578
Why have you been hanging
around me for ten years

40:14.661 --> 40:16.705
eating nothing but fried dumplings?

40:18.665 --> 40:19.791
What do you mean, why?

40:19.875 --> 40:21.460
I went because
the fried dumplings are delicious.

40:23.587 --> 40:24.630
- Is that so?
- Yes.

40:26.256 --> 40:28.258
Right. That's what I expected you to say.

40:29.927 --> 40:30.969
This here.

40:31.762 --> 40:34.264
It's been a while since I've used this.
I wonder if it'll still work.

40:36.099 --> 40:37.100
You know

40:37.184 --> 40:39.311
this is what the guys at the CIA use.

40:40.187 --> 40:41.772
It's a truth serum.

40:41.855 --> 40:44.650
One shot of this,
and you'll spill everything you know.

40:46.109 --> 40:47.903
It was probably
because of all those criminals

40:47.986 --> 40:49.571
wasting time, pleading the fifth
or whatever

40:49.655 --> 40:51.615
that they got pissed off
and developed this in secret.

40:51.698 --> 40:53.533
The effect is amazing.

40:54.242 --> 40:56.536
There's just one unfortunate side effect.

40:59.206 --> 41:00.666
If you're unlucky

41:00.958 --> 41:02.709
there's about a 50%...

41:04.127 --> 41:05.128
chance.

41:09.341 --> 41:10.425
You get me?

41:11.134 --> 41:14.012
- I'll get dizzy?
- You'll spend your life drooling.

41:15.931 --> 41:16.932
No!

41:18.016 --> 41:20.018
Stay away. I said stay away,
you son of a bitch!

41:20.102 --> 41:21.895
Hey! You bastard!

41:21.979 --> 41:24.606
Stop it! Hey, don't do it!

41:26.608 --> 41:28.026
I almost died!

41:30.988 --> 41:32.239
Don't do it.

41:32.531 --> 41:34.116
Stop! You're not really going
to inject me, are you?

41:34.199 --> 41:35.534
I'll ask you one last time.

41:35.617 --> 41:36.910
This is driving me crazy.

41:37.244 --> 41:38.245
Who are you really?

41:38.328 --> 41:40.330
I just went because the fried dumplings
were delicious!

41:41.915 --> 41:43.458
The dumplings were delicious, you say?

41:43.834 --> 41:46.545
Those fried dumplings
you've been eating for ten years...

41:46.920 --> 41:49.923
are just factory-made
frozen dumplings, you idiot.

41:50.841 --> 41:53.468
Well, then I guess the frozen ones
must be really delicious.

41:53.552 --> 41:56.722
- This will sting a bit. Hang in there.
- Don't.

41:56.805 --> 41:58.056
Just bear with it.

41:58.140 --> 42:00.225
- Just bear with it. It's okay.
- Don't. Just...

42:00.475 --> 42:01.768
No, don't do it!

42:04.354 --> 42:05.939
Don't! Wait!

42:06.189 --> 42:07.399
Hwasan Sect!

42:07.482 --> 42:09.317
- Hwasan Sect!
- Hwasan Sect?

42:09.609 --> 42:11.653
The ones who were arrested
for murdering Director Kwon.

42:11.737 --> 42:12.779
Hwang Hwa-san's Hwasan Sect?

42:12.863 --> 42:14.031
That was a frame-up!

42:14.114 --> 42:16.575
We were framed by that bastard
Han Gyeong-wook too!

42:19.202 --> 42:21.121
Stop beating around the bush
and tell me straight.

42:21.204 --> 42:22.789
Ten years ago, when you were on the ferry

42:22.873 --> 42:24.124
I was there too.

42:30.964 --> 42:32.674
Han Gyeong-wook gave us an order

42:32.758 --> 42:34.009
to retrieve the package.

42:34.634 --> 42:36.678
So you were the one
who interfered that day?

42:36.762 --> 42:37.763
That's right!

42:38.263 --> 42:40.474
But things went south, seriously.

42:42.142 --> 42:45.437
We were supposed to intercept the package
that this "Bulgae" was after

42:46.438 --> 42:47.898
and use it to take down Han Gyeong-wook

42:47.981 --> 42:50.025
for what he did to our Chairman!

42:55.363 --> 42:56.406
We were...

42:56.865 --> 42:59.034
are victims of that bastard
Han Gyeong-wook.

42:59.826 --> 43:01.328
After that incident ten years ago

43:01.578 --> 43:03.121
do you have any idea
what happened to the Hwasan Sect?

43:03.371 --> 43:04.581
Watch out!

43:13.715 --> 43:14.716
Boss!

43:14.800 --> 43:15.801
Boss!

43:16.426 --> 43:18.553
Han Gyeong-wook...
He worked with Yoo In-gu

43:18.637 --> 43:20.555
and set me up.

43:21.098 --> 43:22.933
I guess this is the end
for the Hwasan Sect.

43:23.016 --> 43:24.309
It's not over yet!

43:25.102 --> 43:26.937
That National Intelligence Service agent
who got in our way...

43:27.687 --> 43:29.731
- He's on Yeongseon Island right now.
- Goodness...

43:29.815 --> 43:30.816
- Yeongseon Island?
- Yes.

43:30.899 --> 43:33.151
The item that guy, Bulgae
or whatever, is looking for...

43:33.360 --> 43:34.694
We saw him go in to find it

43:34.778 --> 43:36.530
with our own two eyes, Boss.

43:36.613 --> 43:38.949
The item that Han Gyeong-wook
was so desperate to find...

43:39.032 --> 43:40.575
If we can just get our hands on it...

43:45.163 --> 43:46.373
You guys.

43:46.456 --> 43:49.751
Go back to Yeongseon Island
and find that item, understand?

43:50.502 --> 43:51.837
We'll meet again.

43:51.920 --> 43:53.964
Go. Go on.

43:55.465 --> 43:56.925
Hey! Get them now!

43:57.342 --> 43:59.010
- Hurry!
- Yes, sir.

44:00.762 --> 44:03.140
To clear our Boss's name...

44:03.473 --> 44:05.058
and rebuild the Hwasan Sect

44:05.392 --> 44:07.644
finding that item was our only hope.

44:09.980 --> 44:11.815
So, Jeong Ho-myeong.

44:12.691 --> 44:15.485
Since Jeong Ho-myeong
is the best agent in the NIS

44:15.944 --> 44:17.320
he'd find the item. Or rather...

44:17.988 --> 44:18.989
he'd find it for us.

44:22.117 --> 44:23.118
Damn it!

44:25.287 --> 44:26.288
Boss.

44:26.705 --> 44:28.165
It's been three months already.

44:28.415 --> 44:31.126
How long are we going to just sit here
and watch him fool around?

44:31.585 --> 44:34.504
If we jump the gun and screw up like
last time, are you gonna take the blame?

44:36.339 --> 44:37.883
He may not look like much

44:37.966 --> 44:40.218
but he's the top black ops agent
for the National Intelligence Service.

44:40.302 --> 44:42.888
There's a reason he went undercover
at that Chinese restaurant.

44:44.389 --> 44:46.474
All we have to do is jump him

44:46.558 --> 44:47.726
the moment he gets the item.

44:50.854 --> 44:52.856
Yeah, I just had to wait.

44:53.440 --> 44:57.068
That delivery guy must have
some grand plan to be acting like that.

44:57.527 --> 44:59.404
There's no way he's just sitting
on his hands for no reason.

45:00.071 --> 45:03.283
There must be a way to find the item...

45:04.034 --> 45:05.911
...at the restaurant.
That's why he's there.

45:06.703 --> 45:08.163
Every single day, 365 days a year

45:08.246 --> 45:11.166
I waited endlessly, praying and praying.

45:11.249 --> 45:13.251
Praying that Jeong Ho-myeong
would finally make his move.

45:13.335 --> 45:15.337
Praying for a way out of this hell.

45:16.671 --> 45:17.714
But you...

45:18.381 --> 45:21.593
you were too busy playing house
with the\ restaurant owner's daughter.

45:21.676 --> 45:23.136
You didn't seem to care
about finding the item at all.

45:23.220 --> 45:24.679
You looked so happy, didn't you?

45:24.763 --> 45:26.556
CONVENIENCE STORE FOR FREE NO KEY MONEY
PLEASE, JUST TAKE OVER

45:27.599 --> 45:29.643
You think I wanted to start working
at a convenience store?

45:30.560 --> 45:32.520
I had to do something to get by.

45:32.604 --> 45:33.772
This is all...

45:34.314 --> 45:35.815
your fault, Jeong Ho-myeong!

45:44.616 --> 45:48.036
- Is he crazy?
- What a load of crap.

45:48.161 --> 45:49.829
Still, that doesn't make sense.
For ten years...

45:50.330 --> 45:52.332
- So gangsters ran a convenience store?
- What about you?

45:52.624 --> 45:53.959
The so-called top agent at the NIS

45:54.042 --> 45:55.919
- is running a Chinese restaurant?
- What?

45:56.044 --> 45:57.212
And how was I supposed to know

45:57.295 --> 45:58.964
I'd be stuck as a convenience store clerk
for ten years?

45:59.297 --> 46:01.633
Jeong Ho-myeong,
you're supposed to be the NIS's top agent.

46:01.967 --> 46:04.511
None of this would've happened
if you'd just found the item in time!

46:04.594 --> 46:05.595
You son of a bitch.

46:05.679 --> 46:06.972
Are you blaming me for this?

46:07.138 --> 46:08.348
You think I enjoyed living like this?

46:08.431 --> 46:09.474
-You seemed to be enjoying it.

46:09.557 --> 46:12.185
Marrying into the family
of a popular restaurant, having a kid...

46:12.269 --> 46:13.561
you looked plenty happy to me.

46:13.645 --> 46:16.523
A lot happier than me,
working 12-hour shifts.

46:16.606 --> 46:17.607
Am I wrong?

46:18.650 --> 46:20.902
You little punk. So you were born in 1992?

46:20.986 --> 46:23.029
- Why'd you hit me?
- Show some respect.

46:24.489 --> 46:25.907
Help me.

46:31.371 --> 46:32.372
Please help me.

46:32.455 --> 46:33.498
I'm begging you!

46:49.931 --> 46:51.474
When I think about how you guys

46:51.558 --> 46:52.726
botched the operation ten years ago...

46:52.809 --> 46:54.728
I still want to tear you limb from limb.

46:54.936 --> 46:56.104
But what's the point of going after

46:56.187 --> 46:58.815
a worthless small fry like you now?

46:59.316 --> 47:01.318
I'd rather use you as bait...

47:02.152 --> 47:03.611
to land a bigger fish.

47:03.862 --> 47:05.030
What? Bait?

47:05.363 --> 47:06.906
From now on, you'll do exactly as I say.

47:06.990 --> 47:09.075
What, am I crazy?

47:09.659 --> 47:12.120
Just do it. Quit giving me lip, you punk.

47:13.371 --> 47:14.622
Ugh, seriously.

47:15.707 --> 47:16.708
Sit.

47:17.584 --> 47:18.626
I said, sit!

47:18.752 --> 47:19.753
Good grief.

47:24.174 --> 47:26.926
The two men who were captured
with you yesterday...

47:28.011 --> 47:29.763
The one with the messed-up face...

47:30.889 --> 47:32.724
- is Bulgae.
- What? Bulgae?

47:33.224 --> 47:35.435
Him? Then what about the package?
Did you find it?

47:35.518 --> 47:36.519
No.

47:36.644 --> 47:38.355
You're going to find it. Starting now.

47:39.272 --> 47:41.608
Tail Bulgae and find that package,
one way or another.

47:42.692 --> 47:44.194
Are you out of your mind?

47:44.736 --> 47:45.779
You think I'm actually going to do that?

47:46.029 --> 47:47.113
Be your lackey?

47:49.240 --> 47:50.241
Is that right?

47:52.619 --> 47:54.204
I wonder if you'll still refuse
after seeing this.

47:58.792 --> 48:00.251
Oh, hell.

48:04.172 --> 48:05.215
This video...

48:05.423 --> 48:07.967
How about I send it to every gangster
in every group chat?

48:08.468 --> 48:10.637
No, please. Please, I'm begging you.

48:11.054 --> 48:12.055
Please, just don't do that.

48:12.138 --> 48:13.973
- Then you'll do as I say.
- Okay.

48:14.516 --> 48:18.061
Do that, and I'll pave the way for you
to get your revenge.

48:19.396 --> 48:22.023
Because I have a score
to settle with them too.

48:28.571 --> 48:30.031
I'm the only one who will call you

48:30.115 --> 48:31.741
so answer within exactly ten seconds.

48:31.908 --> 48:33.034
If you're even one second late...

48:34.119 --> 48:35.120
you know what'll happen.

48:47.674 --> 48:49.008
Nam-il, you done packing?

48:50.760 --> 48:51.886
What is this, a midnight run?

48:51.970 --> 48:53.721
Why are we suddenly packing?

48:53.847 --> 48:55.598
You want to get dragged away
and beaten half to death again?

48:56.141 --> 48:57.851
Less talking, more packing.

48:57.934 --> 48:59.060
They may have said three days...

48:59.144 --> 49:01.146
but who knows when those guys
will show up again.

49:01.229 --> 49:02.230
And where are we supposed to go?

49:02.313 --> 49:04.274
You don't have any money or friends.

49:08.778 --> 49:09.779
Hey!

49:11.614 --> 49:13.533
You wouldn't know,
but plenty of people would take me in.

49:14.117 --> 49:15.743
Fine, then go to one of those places.

49:16.369 --> 49:17.370
I'll just stay with my friends.

49:17.454 --> 49:19.330
You lost our house running around
with those damn friends

49:19.414 --> 49:20.415
and you want to go to them?

49:21.040 --> 49:22.292
Stop talking nonsense and just pack.

49:22.375 --> 49:24.836
Come on, we have to go
before it gets any later.

49:29.257 --> 49:30.258
So...

49:31.009 --> 49:32.010
where are we going, then?

49:43.855 --> 49:44.856
We're here.

49:51.779 --> 49:52.780
Put our stuff over here.

49:52.864 --> 49:54.699
That way, people can walk by
and not even notice.

49:57.994 --> 50:01.456
The only place you could find
was a closet in the company cafeteria?

50:01.539 --> 50:02.874
What?

50:02.957 --> 50:04.542
It's nice and cozy.

50:05.168 --> 50:06.252
If you take a nap here

50:06.336 --> 50:07.378
you'll sleep like a log.

50:12.133 --> 50:14.677
What are we, parasites?

50:14.928 --> 50:16.679
We should've just gotten a motel.

50:18.431 --> 50:19.891
Stop being so spoiled.

50:20.225 --> 50:21.726
We have to save every last penny

50:21.809 --> 50:23.436
if we want to get our house back.

50:26.439 --> 50:27.440
But if we get caught

50:27.524 --> 50:28.900
aren't you going to get fired?

50:29.692 --> 50:31.361
What's the difference
between clocking in tomorrow

50:31.444 --> 50:32.946
and just coming in a little early today?

50:33.071 --> 50:34.405
Stop whining

50:34.489 --> 50:35.573
and just get inside.

51:11.526 --> 51:13.653
- The ingredients for today are prepped.
- Okay.

51:13.861 --> 51:15.488
- I'll leave the lunch service to you.
- What?

51:15.572 --> 51:17.574
To me? Hey, wait.

51:17.657 --> 51:20.285
First, we have two targets to keep an eye
on.

51:20.618 --> 51:23.121
First, there's Yoo In-gu,
Han Gyeong-wook's right-hand man.

51:23.746 --> 51:25.498
Currently the boss of the Ingu Sect

51:25.582 --> 51:27.125
and the president of Heaven Capital.

51:27.542 --> 51:29.294
There's a reason he's running
his loan shark business

51:29.377 --> 51:31.254
specifically on Yeongseon Island.

51:31.963 --> 51:35.008
I'm going to dig into his background
and figure out his goal.

51:35.383 --> 51:36.676
Next up, Bulgae.

51:36.759 --> 51:38.219
Former North Korean special agent.

51:38.303 --> 51:40.096
His current alias is Bong Je-sun.

51:40.179 --> 51:41.764
According to our intel,
for the past ten years

51:41.848 --> 51:42.890
he's been living on Yeongseon Island

51:42.974 --> 51:44.976
with Heo Bong-pil
and his grandson, Nam-il.

51:45.310 --> 51:46.644
Heo Bong-pil has since passed away

51:46.728 --> 51:49.105
and now he lives alone with Nam-il,
a high school student.

51:49.439 --> 51:50.732
Currently...

51:50.982 --> 51:54.402
he's a manager at Yeongseon Steel,
a rebar processing plant.

51:54.944 --> 51:56.154
This guy...

51:56.237 --> 51:57.947
Ma Gong-bok, you're good at
digging into people's pasts.

51:58.031 --> 51:59.115
You'll take this one.

52:00.617 --> 52:01.618
Oh, man.

52:01.701 --> 52:04.454
He tells people he has amnesia

52:04.537 --> 52:06.497
but it's highly likely just an act.

52:07.206 --> 52:09.250
Thoroughly figure out his true intentions

52:09.334 --> 52:12.045
and finding the item is our objective.

52:12.545 --> 52:15.923
Oh, please. Please, just leave it. Please!

52:17.925 --> 52:22.513
No. Oh, come on.

52:26.392 --> 52:28.519
If you need anything, just give me a call.

52:33.274 --> 52:34.609
- Gong-bok.
- Oh, you're back?

52:34.692 --> 52:37.028
- I ran the numbers.
- Right. Thanks for your hard work.

52:38.237 --> 52:39.906
We're short exactly 300 won!

52:46.704 --> 52:47.705
YEONGSEON FOOD

52:48.748 --> 52:50.041
Boss, I'm dragging her with me.

52:51.167 --> 52:52.168
Honey!

52:53.127 --> 52:54.796
Let's do this in one go, huh?

52:54.962 --> 52:56.130
I'm sorry.

52:57.465 --> 52:58.800
Out of the way.

53:00.593 --> 53:02.970
Stop struggling, damn it. Good.

53:03.054 --> 53:04.347
That's it.

53:10.978 --> 53:12.522
So, these guys

53:12.605 --> 53:14.982
are threatening people who have gambling
debts and took out loans

53:15.066 --> 53:17.485
and buying up all the land
they can on Yeongseon Island.

53:18.945 --> 53:19.946
Hey, thug.

53:20.029 --> 53:23.324
You must have a reason
for extorting people like this, right?

53:23.908 --> 53:25.576
- Spit it out.
- Oh, come on.

53:26.119 --> 53:28.287
Don't lump us in with scum like Yoo In-gu.

53:28.371 --> 53:29.706
Our main business was nightlife.

53:29.831 --> 53:31.708
We never got our hands dirty
with business like this.

53:31.791 --> 53:33.501
So what if your business was different?

53:33.584 --> 53:35.128
You were still thugs,
so you must know something.

53:35.211 --> 53:36.295
Can't you tell just by looking?

53:36.587 --> 53:39.382
It's a classic property holdout scheme
you see in redevelopment zones.

53:39.465 --> 53:41.759
They snatch up cheap land
for next to nothing

53:41.884 --> 53:43.219
and once it's designated a
redevelopment zone

53:43.302 --> 53:45.722
they sell high and cash out.
A classic holdout.

53:45.972 --> 53:47.515
So you're saying
what these guys are doing is

53:47.598 --> 53:49.600
just a simple redevelopment scheme?

53:49.684 --> 53:51.018
Well...

53:51.394 --> 53:53.062
but something about it does seem fishy,
right?

53:53.688 --> 53:55.231
I mean, if it were land
in Gangnam, Seoul, I'd get it.

53:55.314 --> 53:58.067
But how much can land on Yeongseon Island
be worth? Why go through the trouble?

53:58.151 --> 53:59.527
There doesn't seem
to be much profit in it.

54:00.194 --> 54:01.904
Han Gyeong-wook's main campaign promise is

54:01.988 --> 54:04.073
the large-scale development of Yeongseon
Island.

54:04.407 --> 54:06.534
[They're just trying to get a piece of the
development project.

54:07.952 --> 54:09.912
Aren't they just barking up
the wrong tree?

54:11.456 --> 54:13.833
Do you even know who Han Gyeong-wook is?
How can you say that?

54:14.417 --> 54:17.336
You think he's starting this development
project just to improve Yeongseon Island?

54:17.420 --> 54:18.713
Actually, I don't know.

54:21.132 --> 54:22.759
Right. Anyway, what about Bulgae?

54:35.897 --> 54:37.774
What is this? Jeez.

54:37.857 --> 54:39.942
Who told you to take these pictures? Huh?

54:40.026 --> 54:41.861
What is this? Him eating ramyun?

54:42.403 --> 54:43.613
Why would you take a picture of this?

54:43.696 --> 54:46.532
He's cooped up at the company 24/7.
What do you expect me to do?

54:47.158 --> 54:48.451
After Yoo In-gu took his house

54:48.534 --> 54:50.411
he started hiding out
and living at the company.

54:50.661 --> 54:52.288
He never leaves the office.

54:53.039 --> 54:54.624
Hey, you.

54:54.707 --> 54:58.544
Hey, look at this. Huh?
I have this video scheduled to...

55:01.756 --> 55:03.758
I did everything you asked,
but this is going too far!

55:03.841 --> 55:06.177
That only applies if you actually
put some effort into your investigation.

55:06.594 --> 55:08.346
If you come back with nothing next time,
this video is going straight

55:08.429 --> 55:09.764
to NewTube. Got it?

55:13.142 --> 55:14.644
Do we really have to do this here?

55:14.727 --> 55:17.605
I'm practically a pro at giving baths.
Now, come on.

55:28.074 --> 55:29.367
No way.

55:29.450 --> 55:30.701
You go wash up.

55:30.785 --> 55:34.622
You stink. Your whole body stinks,
you hear me?

55:34.705 --> 55:36.833
I can't sleep because of you.
You smell like crap.

55:36.916 --> 55:37.959
What smell?

55:38.042 --> 55:39.794
I showered just last week!

55:43.172 --> 55:44.173
Bend over.

55:56.394 --> 55:58.271
What are you two doing in here?

56:03.067 --> 56:06.112
So, because of your
nephew's gambling debts

56:06.195 --> 56:08.239
you lost your house to Heaven Capital

56:08.614 --> 56:10.074
and with nowhere to go

56:10.366 --> 56:12.368
you've been hiding out here
at the company?

56:14.453 --> 56:16.497
What were you thinking? Seriously.

56:16.789 --> 56:19.333
Are you trying to find a creative way
to get fired or something?

56:20.543 --> 56:21.544
Manager Lee.

56:23.546 --> 56:24.672
Please, just cut me some slack.

56:25.673 --> 56:27.425
I wouldn't be doing this
if I wasn't desperate.

56:27.884 --> 56:28.885
Just for a little while.

56:29.802 --> 56:31.888
Just until I have enough money
for a new place, okay?

56:31.971 --> 56:33.264
And what if I get in trouble?

56:40.146 --> 56:42.189
If you get caught,
I don't know anything about this.

56:44.275 --> 56:45.526
Manager Lee.

56:46.068 --> 56:49.906
I'll handle it, no matter what.
Manager Lee, thank you so much.

57:00.958 --> 57:02.335
Did you get the exact amount?

57:02.418 --> 57:04.086
Yes, I just barely managed it.

57:05.880 --> 57:06.923
But, boss...

57:07.924 --> 57:09.383
Are you sure about this?

57:10.176 --> 57:12.094
All the money from Heaven Capital
and the Ingu Sect's funds

57:12.178 --> 57:13.930
are in here...

57:14.805 --> 57:18.059
If this goes south, we'll immediately
run out of money for our loans, boss.

57:18.184 --> 57:20.811
Jeez, you have no guts.

57:21.604 --> 57:23.105
Ever heard of high risk, high return?

57:24.023 --> 57:26.901
If this deal goes well, we'll get back ten
times our investment, and then some.

57:27.860 --> 57:31.739
Just you watch and learn
how I built up the Ingu Sect.

57:32.573 --> 57:34.200
- Welcome, boss!
- Yeah.

57:36.369 --> 57:37.370
Boss.

57:37.870 --> 57:40.081
- Where are the Chinese guys?
- They're waiting inside.

58:00.726 --> 58:03.312
President Yoo, you don't disappoint.

58:03.688 --> 58:05.648
You really get things done.

58:07.858 --> 58:09.276
Those guys from the Mainland are so picky

58:09.485 --> 58:11.028
it was a real pain sealing the deal.

58:14.323 --> 58:16.367
- What about the rest of the shipment?
- They're busting their asses making it

58:16.450 --> 58:17.952
because the order's so big.

58:18.327 --> 58:20.538
They'll bring the rest
on the next delivery date.

58:20.788 --> 58:23.332
People in Gangnam
will go crazy for quality like this.

58:23.416 --> 58:24.959
Forget Gangnam.

58:25.042 --> 58:27.420
Now, all the Ingu Sect has to do
is rake in the cash.

58:28.629 --> 58:29.964
All right, good work, President Choi.

58:30.881 --> 58:34.343
Make sure the Mainland guys
know we're off to a great start.

58:34.468 --> 58:36.095
This isn't some mom-and-pop shop.

58:36.178 --> 58:38.014
It's the best drug production line
on the Mainland.

58:38.097 --> 58:40.349
No need to worry, those guys are pros
when it comes to business.

58:40.433 --> 58:42.268
All you need to worry about
is the deal date.

58:43.352 --> 58:45.312
He worries about such useless things.

58:45.396 --> 58:47.690
Something's off. It smells fishy.

58:48.441 --> 58:50.109
Come on, think about it.

58:50.192 --> 58:52.945
What they're doing at the capital firm is
shady enough

58:53.029 --> 58:54.613
but running a jerky factory?

58:56.115 --> 58:58.159
What the hell are they up to?

58:59.076 --> 59:00.995
Hey, isn't the jerky factory just a front?

59:01.579 --> 59:02.872
To drag people there
and beat the crap out of them?

59:02.955 --> 59:04.623
No, I thought so too

59:04.707 --> 59:06.500
but they're actually producing jerky.

59:06.709 --> 59:08.419
Hey, that guy, Yoo In-gu,
took over the Hwasan Sect

59:08.502 --> 59:10.296
and joined forces
with Han Gyeong-wook, right?

59:10.963 --> 59:12.006
Then he must be

59:12.089 --> 59:13.883
acting on Han Gyeong-wook's orders.

59:15.301 --> 59:19.138
What the hell are they doing
on Yeongseon Island? Damn it.

59:19.472 --> 59:20.973
What about that other guy
from the Hwasan Sect?

59:21.390 --> 59:23.517
That Ma Gong-bok guy, is he of any use?

59:23.601 --> 59:25.686
I'm just using him
because I'm short-handed.

59:25.770 --> 59:28.147
I mean, can you really trust
some washed-up gangster?

59:30.191 --> 59:32.568
First Bulgae, and now Yoo In-gu...

59:33.194 --> 59:34.320
Whatever's going on

59:34.403 --> 59:35.696
I need to put an end to it.

59:35.905 --> 59:36.906
Put an end to it?

59:39.450 --> 59:40.910
What are you thinking?

59:43.329 --> 59:44.538
I have a bad feeling about this.

59:44.914 --> 59:46.707
I think it's about time I made a move.

59:46.874 --> 59:48.751
No, no. You can't.

59:48.834 --> 59:50.419
Things are still too uncertain.

59:50.503 --> 59:52.963
Let's move when we have a clearer picture.

59:53.047 --> 59:54.965
No. There's no point in waiting.

59:55.466 --> 59:56.842
What are you going to do then?

59:57.009 --> 59:58.219
I guess...

59:59.011 --> 01:00:00.179
with Yoo In-gu...

01:00:00.679 --> 01:00:02.014
I'll have to have a little chat.

01:00:02.223 --> 01:00:03.224
A talk?

01:00:03.516 --> 01:00:04.517
By yourself?

01:00:05.142 --> 01:00:06.727
When have I ever needed backup?

01:00:10.106 --> 01:00:12.775
Wow, look at how pure and white this is.

01:00:12.858 --> 01:00:16.153
Whoa, this is definitely
top-shelf, boss. Right?

01:00:16.278 --> 01:00:17.279
Hey.

01:00:17.363 --> 01:00:20.825
If we get stuff of this quality
on the next deal

01:00:20.908 --> 01:00:22.827
it'll sell like hotcakes

01:00:23.285 --> 01:00:25.371
and the money
will come rolling in like crazy.

01:00:25.579 --> 01:00:29.125
Then all this cleaning up
Chief Han's messes...

01:00:29.208 --> 01:00:31.293
and groveling will finally be over.

01:00:31.377 --> 01:00:32.545
That's right, boss.

01:00:33.379 --> 01:00:34.380
- Kang-sik.
- Yes.

01:00:34.797 --> 01:00:37.133
Today's deal went well,
so let's go somewhere nice for a change.

01:00:41.846 --> 01:00:44.223
I'm gonna go take a leak
so everyone get ready.

01:00:44.306 --> 01:00:45.307
Yes, sir.

01:00:51.856 --> 01:00:53.357
- Yes, sir.
- Yeah.

01:01:19.592 --> 01:01:21.802
Sounds like you're having some trouble.

01:01:22.344 --> 01:01:24.471
I know a good doctor for prostate issues.

01:01:24.638 --> 01:01:25.639
So...

01:01:26.140 --> 01:01:27.808
want a referral?

01:01:28.976 --> 01:01:29.977
Yoo In-gu?

01:01:32.188 --> 01:01:33.314
Who the hell are you?

01:01:51.040 --> 01:01:52.458
I got piss all over me.

01:01:52.875 --> 01:01:53.918
You're dead.

01:02:02.134 --> 01:02:03.969
Who the hell are you? Who sent you?

01:02:04.053 --> 01:02:05.554
Can't you tell?

01:02:05.638 --> 01:02:07.181
I'm the Masked Racer.

01:02:08.349 --> 01:02:10.142
I'm here to punish scumbags like you.

01:02:10.601 --> 01:02:12.478
The Masked Racer!

01:02:14.605 --> 01:02:17.149
Damn psycho. Is he out of his mind?

01:02:18.484 --> 01:02:20.569
You see, for the past few days

01:02:20.653 --> 01:02:23.280
I've been watching all the shit
you've been pulling.

01:02:23.739 --> 01:02:26.784
And there's something
I just can't seem to wrap my head around.

01:02:27.034 --> 01:02:28.035
So I want to ask you a few questions.

01:02:28.118 --> 01:02:30.246
You bastard! Do you have any idea what
you're getting yourself into?

01:02:40.047 --> 01:02:41.048
Tell me.

01:02:41.507 --> 01:02:43.801
Why you gangster bastards
from the Ingu Sect...

01:02:43.884 --> 01:02:45.970
are running rampant on Yeongseon Island.

01:02:46.428 --> 01:02:49.348
Why are you threatening people
and stealing their homes and land?

01:02:50.224 --> 01:02:53.185
Damn it. You sure are curious...

01:03:06.907 --> 01:03:08.200
Believe it or not

01:03:08.284 --> 01:03:10.202
I'm a humanitarian.

01:03:10.744 --> 01:03:13.122
And just beating you senseless
isn't my style.

01:03:17.001 --> 01:03:18.502
What are you waiting for? Grab it.

01:03:22.923 --> 01:03:24.967
You're dead, you bastard.

01:03:25.467 --> 01:03:26.719
Jeez.

01:03:30.723 --> 01:03:31.724
I think...

01:03:32.725 --> 01:03:35.477
Boss has been gone for a while,
don't you think?

01:03:37.021 --> 01:03:38.188
Should I go check on him?

01:03:41.400 --> 01:03:42.735
This little punk.

01:03:43.736 --> 01:03:46.238
How dare you?
The Boss is taking care of his business.

01:04:00.336 --> 01:04:02.171
I'll ask you one last time.

01:04:02.254 --> 01:04:04.173
What's your purpose on Yeongseon Island?

01:04:04.256 --> 01:04:06.800
I don't know, you psycho bastard!

01:04:16.018 --> 01:04:20.022
You. Do you know
when people are the most truthful?

01:04:20.939 --> 01:04:22.733
It's when they're in pain.

01:04:23.817 --> 01:04:26.236
Okay, I'll talk! I said I'll talk.

01:04:29.156 --> 01:04:30.282
We...

01:04:31.909 --> 01:04:34.370
Our purpose on Yeongseon Island is...

01:04:37.289 --> 01:04:38.415
Screw off.

01:04:53.055 --> 01:04:54.056
What the...

01:04:55.766 --> 01:04:57.226
Damn it.

01:05:05.401 --> 01:05:07.069
Damn it, pick up the phone faster!

01:05:10.697 --> 01:05:12.324
- Yes, Boss.
- Hey, Kang-sik!

01:05:12.616 --> 01:05:14.827
-Yes, Boss.
-Kang-sik, the bathroom, now!

01:05:14.910 --> 01:05:16.912
- Yes, Boss?
- Get your ass to the bathroom, damn it!

01:05:17.329 --> 01:05:18.997
You useless punk, the bathroom!

01:05:20.207 --> 01:05:21.375
Hey, to the bathroom!

01:05:22.167 --> 01:05:24.128
Get to the bathroom, you bastards! Move!

01:05:24.211 --> 01:05:25.879
Yes, sir.

01:05:33.887 --> 01:05:35.514
I know who you are.

01:05:35.597 --> 01:05:37.516
You're that guy whose land I took, right?

01:05:37.599 --> 01:05:39.393
Huh? The Martial Arts Master, right?

01:05:40.561 --> 01:05:41.937
I'm the one asking questions here.

01:05:42.020 --> 01:05:43.814
What is your purpose?

01:05:50.446 --> 01:05:52.239
Hey, you so-called Martial Arts Master.

01:05:52.322 --> 01:05:53.532
You think you're going
to walk away from this? Huh?

01:05:57.453 --> 01:05:58.537
Boss!

01:06:01.290 --> 01:06:02.833
Boss!

01:06:06.503 --> 01:06:07.504
What is that?

01:06:08.255 --> 01:06:09.465
What, does he think he's the hero?

01:06:10.757 --> 01:06:13.677
Hey, you masked bastard.
Now you're dead meat.

01:06:23.437 --> 01:06:26.106
SPECIAL THANKS TO KIM SANG-KYUNG
AND KWON YUL FOR THEIR APPEARANCE

01:06:26.857 --> 01:06:29.234
FIFTIES PROFESSIONALS

01:06:40.746 --> 01:06:42.664
One guy turned the
almighty Ingu Sect upside down?

01:06:42.748 --> 01:06:44.082
He doesn't seem to be an ordinary man.

01:06:45.334 --> 01:06:46.335
Get that masked bastard.

01:06:46.418 --> 01:06:48.170
I said get him!

01:06:48.253 --> 01:06:49.505
Guys, let's go!

01:06:49.588 --> 01:06:52.049
The thugs are here to get you!

01:06:52.257 --> 01:06:54.218
- Hey, get him! Quick!
- Yeongseon Food?

01:06:54.301 --> 01:06:55.719
Let's recruit a gatekeeper.

01:06:55.802 --> 01:06:57.137
Yeah, you bet I'm in.

01:06:57.221 --> 01:06:59.806
- What do you need me to do?
- The Passenger Ship Spy Case.

01:06:59.890 --> 01:07:01.725
- You know who this is, don't you?
- A prosecutor is here!

01:07:01.808 --> 01:07:03.352
- A prosecutor!
- Should we take care of him?

01:07:03.477 --> 01:07:04.770
Give me a call.

01:07:04.853 --> 01:07:06.438
Let's wrap this up.

01:07:06.522 --> 01:07:07.981
I was on that passenger ship.

01:07:08.065 --> 01:07:09.983
If we just do nothing, you're really going
to die, Prosecutor Gang.

01:07:10.067 --> 01:07:11.818
So I need to get moving?

01:07:11.902 --> 01:07:12.945
For the sake of my family

01:07:13.028 --> 01:07:14.571
there's nothing I wouldn't do.
